 {:db/id "q-1393" :question/id #uuid "f2ea4789-04ff-53b9-83f0-42f591cf2261" :question/math-academy-id "q-1393" :question/problem "Let $u=⟨4,5,-1⟩$ and $v=⟨-6,0,2⟩.$ Find $u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 5 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-6))j+(4\\cdot 0-5\\cdot (-6))k \\\\  & =(10-0)i-(8-6)j+(0-(-30))k \\\\  & =10i-2j+30k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-1393/ma-source-field/4ae5bfc96528d5c04a8e136fcbefed1fc26a423555d8264fe7e3843cd4530840"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
