 {:db/id [:question/id #uuid "07c1a1e5-eac4-585d-8460-669cc1e39819"] :question/problem "| $x$ | **$-2$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients  of the line $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above can be found using linear regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$-2$** | **$-1$** | **$0$** | **$1$** | **$2$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-139517/ma-source-field/e96e78a16d1c8385a539fedd33529242f7970904bda0606e077a158d9ebf0103"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
