 {:db/id "q-139655" :question/id #uuid "1a930223-bab4-5e61-88ed-049c16fa689a" :question/math-academy-id "q-139655" :question/problem "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-20$ | $-10$ | $40$ | $20$ | $10$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the curve $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}$ that best fits the data above can be found using polynomial regression as \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y,\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector. Which of the following is the observation vector $y$ in this context?" :question/worked-solution "| $x$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-20$ | $-10$ | $40$ | $20$ | $10$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the curve \n\n$$\ny={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x+{\\beta }_{2}{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\overset{^}{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & {1}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 2 & {2}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 3 & {3}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {4}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 5 & {5}^{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-139655/ma-source-field/d48997a63f95cd484a3ca97a60707ce05a235a81b215783feef4dd77157fd001"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
