 {:db/id "q-142915" :question/id #uuid "0a2eced6-9cd5-5469-b3dc-6168e1ec698d" :question/math-academy-id "q-142915" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=P(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=x\\,|\\,Y=4)=\\frac{P(X=x,Y=4)}{P(Y=1)}=\\frac{f(x,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal distribution of $Y.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.35$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ | $0.45$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.2$ | $0$ | $0.2$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.75$ | $0.25$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $x\\in {0,1,2},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.25}=0.4 \\\\ P(X=1\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(1,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0.15}{0.25}=0.6 \\\\ P(X=2\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(2,4)}{{f}_{Y}(4)}=\\frac{0}{0.25}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $0$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142915/ma-source-field/51bdeffb16bdddbd911838082f56dd505114a44812dbc44e27ab46e20533d5f9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
