 {:db/id "q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c" :answer-field/id #uuid "232c8a87-8c1b-58ee-be3e-6552e315bf0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c/54c440c87bfac170fb571553d8a24a6cfa16ca350b5c2b3f7368a702e62c1f54" "q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c/84b9948c0594d46213d0f80a8c681c3f2ef9dfc5db7c72ea3a30ffca2f8eeb14" "q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c/42283953c8840451c0dabaa977d065000307a3c7b193b0a412d7ee4f7781ad7a" "q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c/fd14e6b9760fd82e7f0d484213e2cbe6b97f369ab21e8ed73824bff9248a48b2" "q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c/282bf078296bd89bae9ec7c6f42173ea23c7ae9d16fcff8bc6ba4755ac0837aa"] :answer-field/correct "q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c/fd14e6b9760fd82e7f0d484213e2cbe6b97f369ab21e8ed73824bff9248a48b2" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-142928" :question/id #uuid "d63f5e38-dd7f-5597-b7d6-4c39a2fe3945" :question/math-academy-id "q-142928" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ |\n\nFind the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the following set of conditional probabilities:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=0)\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=y\\,|\\,X=0)=\\frac{P(X=0,Y=y)}{P(X=0)}=\\frac{f(0,y)}{{f}_{X}(0)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distributions for $X$ and $Y$ correspond to the row and column totals, respectively. So, let's compute these:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.3$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.5$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $0.5$ | $0.15$ | $0.35$ | $1$ |\n\nTherefore, for $y\\in {0,2,4},$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=0) & =\\frac{f(0,0)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.5}=0.4 \\\\ P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=2) & =\\frac{f(0,2)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.1}{0.5}=0.2 \\\\ P(X=0\\,|\\,Y=4) & =\\frac{f(0,4)}{{f}_{X}(0)}=\\frac{0.2}{0.5}=0.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the conditional probability mass function can be represented by the following table:   \n\n| $y$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.4$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-142928/ma-source-field/3c2bdcb6b320909709bd92b5c4a0a8fcb0380e1afbe9a3610edc42968b3ebb5c"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
