 {:db/id "q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "4527b519-e235-578b-ba4e-e12b67a2bec9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec/32fb54a3131da38e75fa482fda87c74dc3f9edaa593126c91abf9c23df7059de" "q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec/9f1e9de73fa6f93a0fef31ae0f8baed6a853a3261437aa07ac5a52ef3823fac5" "q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec/d926fcca1bf87ec8be3338b3888eda9d862313126e919d4f2ebcfd7ef2629cca" "q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec/74ad83bf45fdfc3dd9468e5f5c4e0e4ee351bdead489bd6c7ae00836e67513d4" "q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec/d9083c443bffdb906b79f7a2c0d4feebc38aa72f548bf00a8b4d0ebd09e77184"] :answer-field/correct "q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec/d9083c443bffdb906b79f7a2c0d4feebc38aa72f548bf00a8b4d0ebd09e77184" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-143034" :question/id #uuid "b30d46be-646e-5361-a604-5fb66c710b5b" :question/math-academy-id "q-143034" :question/problem "The value $V$ of a particular art object increases with time. The rate of change of the object's value is proportional to the square of the value. What differential equation describes the change of the value at time $t?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **value** $V$ of a particular art object **increases** with time. The **rate** of change of the object's value is **proportional** to the **square of the value**.  *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *value* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ is *proportional to* the *value squared.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}∝{V}^{2}.\n$$\n\nRecall that $∝$ means \"is proportional to.\"\n\n- Finally, we want to replace the proportionality symbol with an equality symbol. Let $k$ be a positive constant. Since the value *increases* with time, our derivative should be *positive*. Therefore, we can rewrite our proportionality statement as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=k{V}^{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143034/ma-source-field/f9a32e443e089f1e669b5c7d60feca2959aa372de1b14c3b09aa92e2b22117ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
