 {:db/id "q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3031e52c-a4c8-5e7c-bd98-d40e649d233d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e/c8a570a7a45299d6bca7534749498af91d95f2281bdd8454030e707cf44ee838" "q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" "q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e/46070df805b4653a5d877039a93fbcfb0cf7186aafc46672fa7e330153961054" "q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e/a3c72559d7d25083af41603553dab28f112bf464761c0eb8d3b6e870c70cfb9e" "q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e/6ec7f55390e84a805c2f4b28c93f893967d5f7a64eeb901750d34dda29cf16f4"] :answer-field/correct "q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-149548" :question/id #uuid "8fb709d8-90a5-57a1-95a3-b0285559ae32" :question/math-academy-id "q-149548" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=(1-x)(y+2)^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>-2$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-2$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=1$ and $y=-2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/34/345665733b6554a7cea9b54a4ca4e93b6d478d67231cfaf3f6180cf0a75c4b1a.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/40/4058b0f027297faf71756da7cad372b76aae980657f053b95318115889c1d614.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $1-x$ | $(y+2)^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(0,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(2,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(0,-3)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(2,-3)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/fc/fc54a4044465d485d4eb55aa8dd81c0e952e8dd56528bc2874bcc67dcffbf3c8.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>-2$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-2$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-149548/ma-source-field/fc0d9ff831816647794a45dca02bc332eff4d0905d23b80df6bdc2a88765ee3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
