 {:db/id "q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21" :answer-field/id #uuid "76abc781-4035-5b2a-a16f-c1906efb7a8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21/c8a570a7a45299d6bca7534749498af91d95f2281bdd8454030e707cf44ee838" "q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" "q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21/bab4acf5ca3a66ed4f11bbcf7574627e6848417923ee89f9393917451c190309" "q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21/46070df805b4653a5d877039a93fbcfb0cf7186aafc46672fa7e330153961054" "q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21/6ec7f55390e84a805c2f4b28c93f893967d5f7a64eeb901750d34dda29cf16f4"] :answer-field/correct "q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21/e4d5cbdd1dc7cc0dd0fdf2a9056c717b9f60123484c35fc7a65c937abab9db2f" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-149597" :question/id #uuid "afec7be1-a030-5a5f-9c4a-b2879ec96690" :question/math-academy-id "q-149597" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=-{x}^{3}{y}^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$ \n\n| $y>0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/93/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-{x}^{3}$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/74/743df5f5c9232346866a01aed9afa3d41fff0f61bf7812b7ae5db9a43efe59f4.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-149597/ma-source-field/c8b40590e5949900125d79523888286d88b269be3affeb787a636749cfd43c21"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
